    137:| AHK matroid Hodge log-concavity of arithmetic prime-divisibility transversal matroid (ATTACK_VECTORS §D31) | FAIL | I | B-grade mode I closure. Built the **arithmetic transversal matroid** `M_P^N` (ground = `[2, N]`, blocks `B_p = {n in [2, N] : p | n}` for primes `p ≤ N`, rank = max bipartite matching to blocks); computed characteristic polynomial via Whitney expansion `χ_M(t) = Σ_{S ⊆ E} (−1)^{|S|} t^{r(M)−r(S)}` over all `2^{|E|}` subsets at `N ∈ {8, 12, 16, 20}`. AHK 2018 *Annals* 188 = arXiv:1511.02888 log-concavity inequality `|w_k|² ≥ |w_{k−1}|·|w_{k+1}|` verified empirically across ~200 matroids (zero violations, sanity check). Compared the AHK slack `δ_k := |w_k|² − |w_{k−1}|·|w_{k+1}|` of the prime matroid to **degree-preserving configuration-model controls** (matching bipartite degree sequence on both sides via stub-pairing). At `N = 20` (50 controls), prime `|w_k|` values exceed config-model means by 3-4×, with z-scores `+2.55σ to +3.44σ` on individual coefficients and `+2.85σ to +5.61σ` on slack. **W-trick attenuation**: `W = 2` (odd integers, odd primes only) reduces deviation to a uniform `+3.17σ` across all coefficients (variance is 1-dimensional in control ensemble); `W = 6` collapses the matroid to free `U_{6,6}` for `N ≤ 20` (need `N ≥ p²` for `p ≥ 5` for non-trivial test). **Direct-sum decomposition**: `M_P^N = M_conn^N ⊕ U_{1,1}^{ν(N)}` where `ν(N) = π(N) − π(N/2)` (Bertrand prime count) and the `U_{1,1}` factors are isolated edges from primes `p ∈ (N/2, N]` (each appears only as itself in `[2, N]`). The `(t-1)^{ν(N)}` factor inflates `|w_k|`; config-model destroys these isolated edges by stub-pairing single-stub right-nodes. **D31.a sub-experiment** (CLOSED in S149): re-ran on connected part `M_conn^N` only (50 controls); deviation reduces by `0.5–1.0σ` but **does not erase**: conn-only `δ_1` z = `+3.91σ` at `N = 20`, individual `|w_k|` z = `+2.41σ to +2.88σ`. Bertrand factor accounts for ~50% of full-matroid deviation; ~50% is residual structure of `M_conn^N` not yet identified analytically (plausibly tied to multiplicative-coincidence 4-cycle structure `Σ_{p<q ≤ √N} (N/(pq))²`). Connected-part char polys (rank 4): `χ_{M_conn^{16}} = 20 − 42t + 30t² − 9t³ + t⁴`, `χ_{M_conn^{20}} = 36 − 70t + 44t² − 11t³ + t⁴`. Pre-stated falsifiers: (E) `±2σ` after W-trick — **NOT achieved**; (I) `≥3σ` deviation, structurally identified — **achieved (+5.6σ at k=1 full, +3.9σ at k=1 conn)**, half-traced to Bertrand; (A) closed-form HL-product `χ_{M_conn^N}` — not pursued (D31.b open). New shape edge **E2.24**: 7th orthogonal pseudorandomness-detection category after Gowers / Anderson / DPP / PH / subword / Mahler / Newman; structurally distinct from E7.17 graph-Laplacian Hodge L_1 (S126, D22) — Chow ring `A^*(M)` and Hodge-Riemann form on graded pieces vs. Hodge Laplacian eigenvalue spectrum. Cross-domain technique: **AHK matroid Hodge theory / Heron-Rota-Welsh log-concavity** (Adiprasito-Huh-Katz 2018 arXiv:1511.02888; Heron 1972 / Rota 1971 / Welsh 1976; Brändén-Huh 2020 *Annals* 192 Lorentzian polynomials = arXiv:1902.03719; Huh 2012 *J. AMS* 25; Edmonds-Fulkerson 1965 transversal matroids). PROPOSED → USED I, edge E2.24. Channelled mathematician: Huh / Adiprasito (combinatorial Hodge). Two open follow-ups (D31.b/c): (b) `χ_{M_conn^N}` HL-product fingerprint at `N ∈ {32, 48, 64}` via deletion-contraction + matroid representation matrix, fit `|w_k|^? = ∏_{p ≤ N^{α_k}} f(p)`; (c) AHK Hodge applied to the χ_P-driven flag matroid of the coprimality complex (S126 / E7.17 closure), structurally distinct matroid class (Björner-Wachs 2007 *Adv. Math.* 207 shellability + Stanley-Reisner ring). See `experiments/algebraic/d31_ahk_matroid_hodge/`, `archive/sessions/session149_d31_ahk_matroid_hodge.md`. | 149 |
    138:| Cohn-Elkies / Delsarte LP bound on chi_P (ATTACK_VECTORS §D29) | FAIL | E | B-grade negative-shape closure (mode E). Wild-swing single-session attempt at the discrete-Z Cohn-Elkies / Delsarte-LP density bound (Cohn-Elkies 2003 *Annals* 157 = arXiv:math/0110009; Viazovska 2017 *Annals* 185 = arXiv:1603.04246; framework re-cast as Delsarte 1973 / Schrijver 2005 SDP arXiv:math/0405348). LP: maximize f_hat(0)=f(0)+2 Σ f(t) subject to f_hat(xi)>=0 (Bochner, M=4096 sample points), f(0)=1, Σ_{t≥1} g(t) f(t) ≤ 0 with g=R_P(t)/π(N) (autocorrelation). Bound: π(N)/N ≤ 1/f_hat^*(0). At N∈{10^4,10^5,10^6}, T_max=500: 1/f_hat^*(g_obs)∈{0.147, 0.158, 0.158} while ρ=π(N)/N∈{0.123, 0.096, 0.078} — saturation S_N=ρ·f_hat^*(0) decays as 0.835→0.608→0.498 (S_N → 0 like 1/log N, vacuous in the limit). T_max sweep at N=10^6, T∈{50,100,200,400,800,1500} gives clean log-linear fit f_hat^*(0; g_obs) ≈ 1.154 + 0.848·log T (residuals all |.|<0.1, R²>0.999). Implication: matching ρ~1/log N at N=10^6 requires log T~13.66, T~e^13.66~8.6·10^5 ≈ N — i.e. **the LP becomes tight only at T_max ≈ N, super-polylog**. For any T_max=polylog(N) the bound is loose by factor log N. Optimal f^* is NOT a Viazovska modular form: residue-mod-4 breakdown gives sum f^*(t)|_{t≡0} ≈ +20.6, sum f^*(t)|_{t≡2} ≈ -20.2, sum f^*(t)|_{t≡1,3} ≈ +0.27 — a period-4 sinusoid f^*(t) ≈ A·cos(πt/2)·1_{t even} reflecting the parity barrier (E2.1). f_hat^* concentrates 38× at xi=1/4 over xi=0. Strictly inside sieve barrier (E6.7). Two A-grade criteria (LP saturation + modular f^*) both ruled out cleanly. New negative-shape edge **E2.23**: "Cohn-Elkies/Delsarte LP optimum scales as f_hat^*(0)=O(log T) for prime autocorrelation; loose by factor log N for any T=polylog(N)." Cross-domain technique: linear-programming bounds for codes / sphere packing (Delsarte 1973; Cohn-Elkies 2003 arXiv:math/0110009; Viazovska 2017 arXiv:1603.04246; Bachoc-Vallentin 2008 arXiv:math/0608426; Schrijver 2005 arXiv:math/0405348) — UNUSED before S145, promoted PROPOSED → USED mode E. See `experiments/analytic/cohn_elkies_chi_p/`, `archive/sessions/session145_d29_cohn_elkies_chi_p.md`. | 145 |
    789:| §D30 ATTACK_VECTORS — Pollicott-Ruelle resonances of χ_P-weighted Gauss-map transfer operator: does L_{χ_P} f(x) = Σ_n χ_P(n) f(1/(x+n))/(x+n)² have an isolated arithmetic resonance encoding π(x), à la Mayer 1991 dynamical-determinant representation of ζ via the unweighted Gauss map? (cross-domain: Pollicott 1985 Inventiones 81 / Ruelle 1976 Inventiones 34 / Mayer 1991 Bull. AMS 25 transfer operator spectral theory; Baladi 2018 *Dynamical Zeta Functions* Springer Ergeb. 68) | FAIL | E | Frontier wild_swing S140 on the FIRST dynamical-spectral / transfer-operator measurement on χ_P, recommended next pick per S139 critique single-pick annotation. Chebyshev-Lobatto barycentric collocation on [0,1], (M_grid+1)-dim matrix; cylinder truncation n_max sweeping {100, 200, 400, 800}; 200 controls per ensemble at M=80, n=400; 5 baselines (B_naive=Bernoulli ρ, B_supp=cardinality-matched random subset of [2..n_max], B_par=parity-matched, B_cra=Cramér 1/log n, B_crao=Cramér+odd-parity most stringent); plus Rademacher controls for Liouville. **Pre-registered falsifiers**: F-A unweighted h=1 reproduces Mayer/GKW spectrum within 1e-3 (sanity); F-B B_crao closure within ±2σ (mode E); F-C ≥3σ deviation persisting under refinement (mode I); F-D closed-form polylog identity (A-grade). **Outcome: B-grade case (i) mode E — F-A passes, F-B holds, F-C/F-D fail.** F-A: top-3 unweighted eigenvalues at M=160, n=800 = (0.99820, -0.30293, +0.10064) vs published GKW (1.0000, -0.30366300289, +0.10088637) — agreement < 0.2% on top-3, sanity ✓. **χ_P spectrum (M=120, n=400)**: |λ_0|=0.35961, |λ_1|=0.05103, |λ_2|=0.00792, |λ_3|=0.00128, |λ_4|=0.00021 — alternating signs, geometric decay (gap |λ_1|/|λ_0|=0.142), parallel to GKW structure. **Refinement-stable**: top-5 eigenvalues vary by <1% CV across (M_grid, n_max) ∈ {30..160}×{100..800}, real Pollicott-Ruelle resonances (not spurious-discretisation). **Closed-form prediction**: leading eigenvector of L_h overlaps unweighted Gauss density g(x)=1/((1+x)log2) at cosine ≥0.9919 for h ∈ {χ_P, λ, Λ}; arithmetic content lives in eigenvalue, not eigenfunction. Rayleigh-quotient closed form λ_0^h ≈ Σ_n h(n)·a_n with a_n=T_n/||g||², T_n=∫₀¹dx/[(1+x)(x+n)(x+n+1)·log²2] explicit (partial fractions); for n≥2: T_n=(1/log²2)·[ln2/(n(n-1)) - ln((n+1)/n)/(n-1) + ln((n+2)/(n+1))/n], asymptotic a_n~2log2/n², Σa_n=1. **At n_max=400: Σ_p a_p = 0.36187 vs measured |λ_0|^{χ_P}=0.35961, +0.6% rel error; Σ_n Λ(n)·a_n = 0.5206 vs measured |λ_0|^Λ=0.4968, +4.8% rel error.** For signed λ Rayleigh fails by factor 2 (left eigenvector ≠ const for signed weights). **Cramér closure**: vs B_crao 200 seeds at M=80, n=400: |λ_0| z=-1.79, |λ_1| z=-1.60, gap z=+2.10 — all within ±2σ Bonferroni (3-feature ≈ 2.39σ); F-B holds. vs B_supp z=+3.58 (uniform random over-spreads to high indices, false depression); vs B_par z=+2.02 (parity matched but lacks log-density profile). **A-grade hypothesis falsified**: |λ_0|/(π(N)/N) = 0.3596/0.195 = 1.844 — NOT a closed-form constant; the closed form IS Σ_p a_p, which is cost-equivalent to enumerating primes ≤ N. **Mechanism for closure mode E**: arithmetic-weighted PR leading resonance is a DENSITY-ONLY invariant at first moment — captured exactly by Σ_n h(n)·a_n where {a_n} is independent of h. Cramér model 1/log n + odd parity reproduces this expectation within sample noise. **Mayer-style dynamical-determinant representation of π(x) NOT opened**: there is no isolated arithmetic resonance distinct from the density-Rayleigh prediction. **Connections**: STRUCTURALLY DISTINCT from E2.13 Gowers (S85 detected HL → W-trick erases), E2.14 Anderson Lyapunov (S88 detected HL → W-trick erases), E2.16 anti-DPP (S95), E2.17 PH (S96), E2.19 subword (S104), E2.20 Mahler (S134), E2.21 Newman (S138) — all DETECT HL deviations; E2.22 (this work) shows the dynamical-spectral leading resonance is a 1-summing density integral that the Cramér model captures by construction. STRUCTURALLY DISTINCT from CLOSED line 320, 425