    812	| S192 critique — audit of S164–S191 batch (S164 D44 Rédei + S82 commit thread closure S165/S166/S168/S169/S190 + S191 paradigm-shift T_Q + 20 verify slots S167/S170-S189) — does the batch contain inflated grades, mis-cited edges, or duplicate `novel/` placements? | CRITIQUE | C | Per-artefact verification of seven production sessions plus 20 verify slots. **Zero new demotions, zero inflations caught**: all seven self-grades honestly placed (six B, one C). **S190's HONEST self-down-grade A/B → C** distinguished as positive discipline signal — cleanest commit-thread closure in project history. **S191's "1.4% L²-match-with-S169" identified as TAUTOLOGICAL** (the construction projects onto exactly the subspaces S168 measures the energy of, so the agreement at the L² level is a definitional sanity check, not a new prediction); the actual B-grade content is the precision-at-π(N) lift table (new pointwise measurement) + d=14/18 missing-spike cross-validation (closes a S169 ambiguity) + L6 Lean candidate. **A-grade scarcity escalated**: S163 flagged 0/20, S192 flags **0/30** A-grades in the rolling window (S162-S191). The frontier-saturation pattern persists: every wild_swing (S164 D44 in this batch) closes at mode E or I via "matches matched-baseline" or "determined by graph/algebraic structure modulo arithmetic-blind invariant". **Recommended next-action**: commit mode → Thread 2 Connes-Consani-Moscovici amortisation (per .commit_state next_thread:connes_amortisation); non-commit → ATTACK_VECTORS §A.A7 plethysm sub-frame (S156's orbit-dim work explicitly leaves it open) OR §D.D48 BC endomotive Galois-orbit (S163 critique-pick still open). **Cadence note**: this is the third consecutive critique (S147, S163, S192) recommending an A-target attempt rather than another refinement; harness has continued to select commit/refinement modes; pattern flagged for human review (not at "≥ 2 F-grades in a row" escalation threshold — all sessions B/C). **No edits to EDGES.md, NOVELTY_CHALLENGES.md, ATTACK_VECTORS.md, or RESEARCH_AGENDA.md**. One trivial citation-drift note in S191 ("S190's 1.18 finite-size factor" should read "S166's"); not worth a separate row. See archive/ephemeral/critique_latest.md and archive/sessions/session192_critique.md. | 192 |
